			"notes": "- Replaced portal grouping with a single global progress counter. All detected portals now contribute to one shared progress meter and one shared target. When the target is reached, one portal lights chosen at random weighted by its per tick probability, then a new target is rolled and progress resets.\n- Each flammable block now burns at its own deterministic time based on its position instead of every block burning at once.\n- Fire placed with flint and steel near a portal now works correctly.\n- Flammables blocks away from the frame now burn correctly, and flammables next to an unlit frame keep burning after the portal lights.\n- Fixed fire being left permanently in the world after a portal frame is destroyed."
		},
